# ── copyrighted source + anything derived from it ──
# Archives are dropped at the PROJECT ROOT. These patterns MUST exist before the first commit —
# a zip committed once lives in git history forever and rewriting history later is miserable.
*.zip
*.rar
*.r00
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.cbz
*.epub
*.djvu
compiler/sources/
compiler/sources/inbox/
compiler/work/
compiler/dist/
**/quarantine.jsonl
*.pdf

# ── build artifacts ──
*.apk
*.aab
app/build/
build-logic/build/
# The ROOT project's own build dir. Gradle writes build/reports/ here (e.g. the configuration-cache
# problems report) even though the root project has no code. Anchored with a LEADING SLASH so it
# matches ONLY this directory at the repo root — see the warning below for why a bare `build/` is
# not safe here.
/build/
.gradle/
local.properties
# ⚠ Do NOT "simplify" the three build lines above into `**/build/` or a bare, unanchored `build/`.
# The guard's own source lives in build-logic/src/main/kotlin/dev/kayomarz/studyfeed/**build**/ — a
# package named `build` — and an unanchored rule would match it, silently stopping new files there
# from ever being committed. `/build/` is anchored to the repo root and does NOT match that package;
# a bare `build/` would match it at any depth and IS unsafe. List output dirs explicitly, one per
# module, anchoring where a name collides with real source.

# ── signing: losing these is bad, committing them is worse ──
*.jks
*.keystore
# The real keystore is PKCS12 (.p12) and lives OUTSIDE this repo entirely (§11d). These patterns
# are belt-and-braces for the day someone copies it in "just for a second".
*.p12
*.pfx
keystore.properties

# ── env / secrets ──
.env
*.env
**/.anthropic_key

# ── python ──
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Android Studio / IntelliJ ──
# Generated the moment the project is opened in the IDE. Machine-specific (SDK paths, JDK choice,
# window layout) — committing them makes the repo depend on one person's IDE setup, which is the
# opposite of the §8 A0 "buildable from the CLI, no IDE-only config" contract.
.idea/
*.iml
.kotlin/
captures/
# local.properties is already ignored above (it holds this machine's sdk.dir).

# ── misc ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# atomic-write temp files for the state file
compiler/.compiler_state.*.tmp

# keep the state file — it has cursors and hashes, no content
!compiler/.compiler_state.json

# ── public snapshot folder (generated by tools/sync-public.sh; its own repo) ──
/public/
